{"title":"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(geometric_interpretation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (geometric interpretation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Condensed_Algebraic_Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Condensed Algebraic Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(substitution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (substitution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Geometric)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Geometric)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1d002db36c51a77f8fbc6314e96756fc793e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers satisfying the system of equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd1ad23505737c199eeef4acc0d2a614788212c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sqrt{2x-xy} + \\sqrt{2y-xy} &amp;= 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2y-yz} + \\sqrt{2z-yz} &amp;= \\sqrt2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2z-zx} + \\sqrt{2x-zx} &amp;= \\sqrt3. \\end{align*}\" width=\"231\" height=\"79\" /> \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1ff4ecc5f5319e77a3c7a3d7e9534a9ec343da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[ (1-x)(1-y)(1-z) \\right]^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"23\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hint\">Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Try to get some restrictions on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> based on the square root that may result in motivation for some trigonometric substitutions.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28geometric_interpretation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(geometric_interpretation)\">Solution 1 (geometric interpretation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (geometric interpretation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, let define a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/72147e728de9b0a5edd0397d5ad7afea27f98ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/00869da7629554bf8ad135794619b9e3a1f2c443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, with altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />'s equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/c/0cc87147ee7293f4c425c54eeb604a526998f637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{xz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b309570e39fbcdddbfa296662aa1f059dfbfc65e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = \\sqrt{2x - xz} + \\sqrt{2z - xz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" />, the left side of one equation in the problem.\n</p><p>Let  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be angle opposite the side with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/72147e728de9b0a5edd0397d5ad7afea27f98ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />. Then the altitude has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/304a4a624f3ea5b78b12db53c3ae68fa3ea466d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2z} \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) = \\sqrt{xz}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"24\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e113ce9df9861a44ca4b585e19121709adc57f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\theta) = \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"104\" height=\"45\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11aed9bd46c75ce5e3eae3c4813210015a098649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2\\sin^2(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"22\" /> and the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/72147e728de9b0a5edd0397d5ad7afea27f98ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef21c3c1f1e4fc5955ec62635dcf4b7ebfa724fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can symmetrically apply this to the two other equations/triangles. \n</p><p>By law of sines, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7768d860dbe6464354940c816e2bcabddc11d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\sin(\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)} = 2R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"111\" height=\"45\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd408b15b2dc884e8559a232ede521f67b511f89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> as the circumradius, same for all 3 triangles. \nThe circumcircle's central angle to a side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f78cba504b3c1369ae10bc750def084ed7c321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\arcsin(l/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, so the 3 triangles' <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5daf0cbd0204b975e8858c97fb63fc538715f8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=1, \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"23\" />,  have angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/11314e9f21364916b44b13877975a4ffcfcd0930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^{\\circ}, 90^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>This means that by half angle arcs, we see that we have in some order, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c293eed29b9ff163440b14e756706bf01500f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2\\sin^2(\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"22\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbedfb0fbf1baf5fe244763445cb55905ae8cb7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2\\sin^2(\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"22\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55a7ce4e0a30aea76eb964a6ae9d9a5cf256e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2\\sin^2(\\gamma)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"22\" /> (not necessarily this order, but here it does not matter due to symmetry), satisfying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f65a41165570be27d0cb4bca601d1a5f94e3e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\beta=180^{\\circ}-\\frac{120^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/32065a927f1e85346cb4bafa6edb895fd962c114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta+\\gamma=180^{\\circ}-\\frac{90^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d284d851231c688446de8ecd9841f454f4e38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma+\\alpha=180^{\\circ}-\\frac{60^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"39\" />. Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6bb42bcf7c1bb37ccb49ba1f0afedba8d0af07b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha=\\frac{135^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f2aac1e857554625039771b16965c808079469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta=\\frac{105^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af809d8ab2ebbec0e35efe01ff05d888e40b580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma=\\frac{165^{\\circ}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d91c6e7f5258ec291c3f9637b04eb9bc4fa19df4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[(1-x)(1-y)(1-z)]^2=[\\sin(2\\alpha)\\sin(2\\beta)\\sin(2\\gamma)]^2=[\\sin(135^{\\circ})\\sin(105^{\\circ})\\sin(165^{\\circ})]^2\\]\" width=\"635\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4806ad451d0248129d657ed966100bf612900876.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{32} \\to \\boxed{033}. \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>- kevinmathz\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Condensed_Algebraic_Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Condensed_Algebraic_Trig)\">Solution 2 (Condensed Algebraic Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Condensed Algebraic Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05911eb946e0704d5d776e76ead7246eb213d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{A} = \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"97\" height=\"45\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c037324821e1d51c4bd329b5885c633a11b2a20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{B} = \\sqrt{\\frac{y}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"97\" height=\"45\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/64293ea4b9f0d24dfea1c4797b1526e63752a8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{C} = \\sqrt{\\frac{z}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"97\" height=\"45\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3ad13be2fbefc387752d4ed08437d21bc61ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C \\in (0^\\circ,90^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />; therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b45fecf775e83bae6d0996c17d67858065010d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{A} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2-x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"131\" height=\"45\" />, etc. Dividing all three given equations by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we see that they are equivalent to\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sin(A+B) &amp;= \\sin(30^\\circ) \\\\\n\\sin(B+C) &amp;= \\sin(45^\\circ) \\\\\n\\sin(C+A) &amp;= \\sin(60^\\circ),\n\\end{align*}\nwhich produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed239d6b53aa7e691b48120f57bf7158d7c7d19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\frac{45}{2}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fef728a1d2ea6a1514a0116bb2c5b7d58780e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\frac{15}{2}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543315a7321520790afcb6d9163681c005bbb282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\frac{75}{2}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"40\" />. Thus our answer is\n\\begin{align*}\n[(1-x)(1-y)(1-z)]^2 &amp;= [(1-2\\sin^2 A)(1-2\\sin^2 B)(1-2\\sin^2 C)]^2 \\\\\n&amp;= (\\cos(2A)\\cos(2B)\\cos(2C))^2 \\\\\n&amp;= \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)^2 \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{1}{32},\n\\end{align*}\nproducing the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9e90592f1e0ca221dd5eb3ce4c1f2121297300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{033}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Remark. Note that liberties have been taken in mathematical rigor in the above solution, especially when dealing with angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and the inverse sine function. However, these details do not affect the overall solution and may be carefully checked during the contest if desired; thus we feel justified in leaving them out to emphasize the elegance of the trigonometric substitution.\n</p><p>~Oxymoronic15 (edited for length by Viliciri)\n~LentaroT (edit for trig values)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(substitution)\">Solution 3 (substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dceff5a6847081e060e4ccdc8be3cae957cabeb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-x=a;1-y=b;1-z=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"18\" />, rewrite those equations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1499c69b6e965648e4aed6b74232364e8cb15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(1-a)(1+b)}+\\sqrt{(1+a)(1-b)}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"310\" height=\"35\" />;\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4ab15319bf711833be1b07aa7553632500af11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(1-b)(1+c)}+\\sqrt{(1+b)(1-c)}=\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"321\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d3a352dccc93bfb4db96464024164f8911fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(1-a)(1+c)}+\\sqrt{(1-c)(1+a)}=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"325\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2b933238108d72a435a8ace1fbce8e8cf1e16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n = (abc)^2 = a^2b^2c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Square both sides and simplify, to get three equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e85c7e3a7f9f57d8fdf1d4e76098dedd393524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ab-1=2\\sqrt{(1-a^2)(1-b^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"234\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbe0efc66f3cb629796d3b38f5ceb4b1d99d4ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2bc~ ~ ~ ~  ~ ~=2\\sqrt{(1-b^2)(1-c^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"232\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2e7bd8094a2d24add5705cdcdbb9bfa636ec83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ac+1=2\\sqrt{(1-c^2)(1-a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"234\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Square both sides again, and simplify to get three equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1dcb7aba40f49f752903ecb74544e0f36ef4f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2-ab=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87fce8574fbcffc2460757bcd301071d1bf710d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2+c^2~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3da7027744f190c891f60a50edb1a4da655d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+c^2+ac=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Subtract first and third equation, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b356a7a46ca989a64b6820be781240a7cbc8ce1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b+c)(b-c)=a(b+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/73865168ef14fd6b0f9ed4678e02967b68e2412c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b-c$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Put it in first equation, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35a3a018bbef6c1c34341bac61911244f2c94c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-2bc+c^2+b^2-b(b-c)=b^2+c^2-bc=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"373\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a253108a30704591ad253a4a7e4b0822e577e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/9036a376b5982ca9c0131c2f96074686228a33ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2=b^2+c^2-2bc=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b4f3ee5e5907effacf5a17b213b2139e8dbc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n = a^2b^2c^2 = a^2(bc)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"322\" height=\"48\" />  and so the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9e90592f1e0ca221dd5eb3ce4c1f2121297300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{033}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22aaed09f8985af3ac28c700530628a50fcf3430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = 1 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2ee12d1b5a58210b19e40df45b8ffa343a454cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = 1 - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa292b37122de764b8e4842c50437681fec23991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = 1 - z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />.\nHence, the system of equations given in the problem can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db1568352d7ab3ca817f83539414175aac1bac8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sqrt{(1-u)(1+v)} + \\sqrt{(1+u)(1-v)} &amp; = 1 \\hspace{1cm} (1) \\\\ \\sqrt{(1-v)(1+w)} + \\sqrt{(1+v)(1-w)} &amp; = \\sqrt{2} \\hspace{1cm} (2) \\\\ \\sqrt{(1-w)(1+u)} + \\sqrt{(1+w)(1-u)} &amp; = \\sqrt{3} . \\hspace{1cm} (3)  \\end{align*}\" width=\"408\" height=\"110\" />\n</p><p>Each equation above takes the following form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d032c3b5cf66b460f7780a71876dc8854d2176fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\sqrt{(1-a)(1+b)} + \\sqrt{(1+a)(1-b)} = k . \\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Now, we simplify this equation by removing radicals.\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d115b22cc61a1e64c4e94e048c241361529c745c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\sqrt{(1-a)(1+b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8101b023dc3b91bb8e5ed88a07c8564b2d6627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = \\sqrt{(1+a)(1-b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, the equation above implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bed99ded09196ed2868510a10f5733e88189934.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l} p + q = k \\\\ p^2 = (1-a)(1+b) \\\\ q^2 = (1+a)(1-b) \\end{array} \\right.. \\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0aac8b16412cd33f07950830f05c9291e2d7fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 - p^2 = (1+a)(1-b) - (1-a)(1+b) = 2 (a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"407\" height=\"21\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98cd4151661cf4d8489bc5449d55bc7bff43d406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q - p = \\frac{q^2 - p^2}{p+q} = \\frac{2}{k} (a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"217\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/78145ab3e6df0c92e4b88600e59d51d7a56b0615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c782ae1fefeafd02289f9d473b698495f0abf1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q - p = \\frac{2}{k} (a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff30c19c7f3d54d3f214926d93bdd0b0b6fa95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = \\frac{a-b}{k} + \\frac{k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"39\" />.\nPlugging this into the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b289b9f3575aa1e900dee42bbd90b7ff728be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 = (1+a)(1-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" /> and simplifying it, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12ef1a1e7fce479cd3b0c59ec2e17fc3999708a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ a^2 + \\left( k^2 - 2 \\right) ab + b^2 = k^2 - \\frac{k^4}{4} . \\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the system of equations above can be simplified as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c490cac41eb79f16404542b2f230e4adfedfd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} u^2 - uv + v^2 &amp; = \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ v^2 + w^2 &amp; = 1 \\\\ w^2 + wu + u^2 &amp; = \\frac{3}{4}  . \\end{align*}\" width=\"147\" height=\"107\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e403c2040a8182cecad5cdcb398b1bb7dc7ab73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w&#39; = - w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />.\nThe system of equations above can be equivalently written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/95783e6036202cd4ada1a81275cf82cd53eca62c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} u^2 - uv + v^2 &amp; = \\frac{3}{4} \\hspace{1cm} (1&#39;) \\\\ v^2 + w&#39;^2 &amp; = 1 \\hspace{1cm} (2&#39;) \\\\ w&#39;^2 - w&#39;u + u^2 &amp; = \\frac{3}{4} \\hspace{1cm} (3&#39;) . \\end{align*}\" width=\"231\" height=\"107\" />\n</p><p>Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f26f45fe802f77b147551904bc58498b2b6526c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1&#39;) - (3&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21f30ce8246569be3f67510cd2008badabfe01d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ (v - w&#39;) (v + w&#39; - u) = 0 . \\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f3cff25bef11a69c81dcb12c363fd734ea98e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v - w&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aecfb47b20d58d63c3b36c2b9cb5ece8d2b0af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v + w&#39; - u = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154c3cf3af5df5469bbb7b40718758979f2bb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 1}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"11\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f3cff25bef11a69c81dcb12c363fd734ea98e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v - w&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Equation (2') implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf17ded18ef242f9ccb7d28ab728571585dcfc31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = w&#39; = \\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/11355298328f1cd40da4c649ccf7d3d07d88b84a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> into Equation (2), we get contradiction. Therefore, this case is infeasible.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901dd3d64f25ed84522adca7c7693a46693cbcf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case 2}$\" width=\"54\" height=\"11\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aecfb47b20d58d63c3b36c2b9cb5ece8d2b0af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v + w&#39; - u = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging this condition into (1') to substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c216f6b8302c120dbe28c5fe62f62228d61d97c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ v^2 + v w&#39; + w&#39;^2 = \\frac{3}{4} \\hspace{1cm} (4) . \\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fcedd646be14bfa3460927a500d526117fd8bee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4) - (2&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e511f67d7e004691412861bb243f8d5e1b01a3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ v w&#39; = - \\frac{1}{4} . \\hspace{1cm} (5) . \\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Taking (4) + (5), we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badc51fb26e150ecdcebc6b2ed2df7265ea60969.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\left( v + w&#39; \\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} . \\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341549b68f396a2a1dda652ba62741df031df5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 = \\left( v + w&#39; \\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7ecd3c2e3fd3f14f21546db474f4dc420c959ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left[ (1-x)(1-y)(1-z) \\right]^2 &amp; = u^2 (vw)^2 \\\\ &amp; = u^2 (vw&#39;)^2 \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( - \\frac{1}{4} \\right)^2 \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{32} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"280\" height=\"147\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c5b930a1d063ccad0ee3f9a7edeb51f2d48714b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 32 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(033) }}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"137\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p>bu-bye\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d17c4ec8f6519c8788864192227e96a33375677.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin(\\alpha + \\beta) &amp;= 1/2 \\\\  \\sin(\\alpha + \\gamma) &amp;= \\sqrt2/2 \\\\  \\sin(\\beta + \\gamma) &amp;= \\sqrt3/2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"151\" height=\"78\" />\nThus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43f0e4ace2a81bf2d51bf00347589a0f0dede48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\alpha + \\beta &amp;= 30^{\\circ} \\\\  \\alpha + \\gamma &amp;= 45^{\\circ} \\\\  \\beta + \\gamma &amp;= 60^{\\circ}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"98\" height=\"67\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f515b97d32d9f90bee1d7cf9bc8fe8ac07ddda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma) = (15/2^{\\circ}, 45/2^{\\circ}, 75/2^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"20\" />. Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0682500d35af9b987fdb70b17a5145c01f826f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[abc = (1-2\\sin^2(\\alpha))(1-2\\sin^2(\\beta))(1-2\\sin^2(\\gamma))=\\cos(15^{\\circ})\\cos(45^{\\circ})\\cos(75^{\\circ})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8},\\]\" width=\"642\" height=\"41\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e9fb9cdebf4f1b70ed223d15b125400a19393d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(abc)^2=(\\sqrt{2}/8)^2=\\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />, for a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9e90592f1e0ca221dd5eb3ce4c1f2121297300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{033}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><u><b>Remark</b></u>\n</p><p>The motivation for the trig substitution is that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49ff813139ec17f65a51c2843066bdb28323f9cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\alpha)=(1-a)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bfb87c13fd4104382976234992afe2194d30d8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2(\\alpha)=(1+a)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />, and when making the substitution in each equation of the initial set of equations, we obtain a new equation in the form of the sine addition formula.\n</p><p>~ Leo.Euler\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Geometric.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Geometric)\">Solution 6 (Geometric)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Geometric)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2022_AIME_I_15.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/2022_AIME_I_15.png/400px-2022_AIME_I_15.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"394\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8e/2022_AIME_I_15.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure> \n<p>In given equations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f6353d4561ae68730e5f41775c30bac8284ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq x,y,z \\leq 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" /> so we define some points:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/162ed1f73e4d8a423d2a810fd6c976ffc9abcbf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bar {O} = (0, 0), \\bar {A} = (1, 0), \\bar{M} = \\left(\\frac {1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac {1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right),\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45ad92aa575c4cc3a19c0ae02b479a693b1c6193.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bar {X} = \\left(\\sqrt {\\frac {x}{2}}, \\sqrt{1 – \\frac{x}{2}}\\right), \\bar {Y&#39;} = \\left(\\sqrt {\\frac {y}{2}}, \\sqrt{1 – \\frac{y}{2}}\\right),\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52fb59194df758e4f8f11fad47055d3f06650c1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bar {Y} = \\left(\\sqrt {1 – \\frac{y}{2}},\\sqrt{\\frac {y}{2}}\\right), \\bar {Z} = \\left(\\sqrt {1 – \\frac{z}{2}},\\sqrt{\\frac {z}{2}}\\right).\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"44\" />\nNotice, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b84b4e10e2862268208652014244483afbe16f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mid \\vec {AO} \\mid = \\mid \\vec {MO} \\mid = \\mid \\vec {XO} \\mid =\\mid \\vec {YO} \\mid = \\mid \\vec {Y&#39;O} \\mid =\\mid \\vec {ZO} \\mid = 1\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"22\" /> and each points lies in the first quadrant.\n</p><p>We use given equations and get some scalar products:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d597b8b9841c19c8d18ec0615e28c39fa3c606d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\vec {XO} \\cdot \\vec {YO}) = \\frac {1}{2} = \\cos \\angle XOY \\implies  \\angle XOY = 60 ^\\circ,\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"37\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff0bf7e1e1b8952c5267420c1deba06613cf3d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\vec {XO} \\cdot \\vec {ZO}) = \\frac {\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\cos \\angle XOZ \\implies  \\angle XOZ = 30^\\circ,\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"41\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6aa63b0c2dd6b8ba2a27dc13bfbe824cdb58aca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\vec {Y&#39;O} \\cdot \\vec {ZO}) = \\frac {1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\cos \\angle Y&#39;OZ \\implies  \\angle Y&#39;OZ = 45^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"415\" height=\"41\" /> \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328c60e14bc41b1dd087d39309992aa398c5181c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YOZ =  \\angle XOY – \\angle XOZ =  60 ^\\circ – 30 ^\\circ = 30 ^\\circ,   \\angle Y&#39;OY =  \\angle Y&#39;OZ +  \\angle YOZ = 45^\\circ + 30 ^\\circ = 75^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"726\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f898155997022cd6259c6a0e0b50802954d80122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c02a4a0d4011b1acc5d4a2045d77783e1f5368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Case 1</b></i>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16827a5b90b6726556df1109a700100bcf67873.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle YOA = \\frac{90^\\circ – 75^\\circ}{2} = 7.5^\\circ, \\angle ZOA = 30^\\circ + 7.5^\\circ = 37.5^\\circ, \\angle XOA = 60^\\circ + 7.5^\\circ = 67.5^\\circ .\\]\" width=\"649\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847fe7107ec14d4993cd65c4aa5aa63ed20bf32b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 – x = \\left(\\sqrt{1 – \\frac{x}{2}} \\right)^2– \\left(\\sqrt{\\frac {x}{2}}\\right)^2  = \\sin^2 \\angle XOA – \\cos^2 \\angle XOA = –\\cos 2 \\angle XOA = –\\cos 135^\\circ,\\]\" width=\"670\" height=\"48\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/8594d5a5cca93ead468401317d8812f097595d33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 – y = \\cos 15^\\circ, 1 – z = \\cos 75^\\circ \\implies  \\left[ (1–x)(1–y)(1–z) \\right]^2 = \\left[ \\sin 45^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 15^\\circ \\cdot \\sin 15^\\circ \\right]^2 =\\]\" width=\"654\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/6366e9e5f9389ebc6bbc3cc823fa9f983bddfce8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left[ \\frac {\\sin 45^\\circ \\cdot \\sin 30^\\circ}{2} \\right]^2  = \\frac {1}{32} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{033}}.\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"46\" />\n<i><b>Case 2</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/971cc162a6a4ef43c09c0c964f8bcef92ca422b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle Y_1 OA = \\frac{90^\\circ + 75^\\circ}{2} = 82.5^\\circ, \\angle Z_1 OA = 82.5^\\circ – 30^\\circ = 52.5^\\circ, \\angle X_1 OA = 82.5^\\circ – 60^\\circ = 22.5^\\circ \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{033}}.\\]\" width=\"784\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/i6kDMbav2sk\">https://youtu.be/i6kDMbav2sk</a>\n</p><p>~Math Gold Medalist\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aa_VY4e4OOM?si=1lHSwY3v7RICoEpk\">https://youtu.be/aa_VY4e4OOM?si=1lHSwY3v7RICoEpk</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihKUZ5itcdA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihKUZ5itcdA</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I\" title=\"2022 AIME I\">2022 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017024112\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.068 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.089 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 746/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1756/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 115/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27370/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.587      1 -total\n 58.23%    7.329      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.08%    5.045      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21793:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 2026101702411